  "description": "PUVYEM crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group C m c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C144 H112 Gd6 N18 Ni6 O44. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.245-3.861 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.71-105.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C144H112Ni6Gd6N18O44. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
